mes>T</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>A randomized, controlled study of a simple, once-daily regimen of                        dihydroartemisinin-piperaquine for the treatment of uncomplicated,                        multidrug-resistant falciparum malaria.</article-title><source>Clin Infect Dis</source><volume>41</volume><fpage>425</fpage><lpage>32</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16028147</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0006358-Smithuis1"><label>8</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Smithuis</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Kyaw</surname><given-names>MK</given-names></name><name><surname>Phe</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Aye</surname><given-names>KZ</given-names></name><name><surname>Htet</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Efficacy and effectiveness of dihydroartemisinin-piperaquine                        versus artesunate-mefloquine in falciparum malaria: an open-label randomised                        comparison.</article-title><source>Lancet</source><volume>367</volume><fpage>2075</fpage><lpage>85</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16798391</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0006358-Karema1"><label>9</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Karema</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Fanello</surname><given-names>CI</given-names></name><name><surname>Van Overmeir</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Van Geertruyden</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>van Doren</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Safety and efficacy of dihydroartemisinin/piperaquine                        (Artekin&#x000ae;) for the treatment of uncomplicated <italic>Plasmodium                            falciparum</italic> malaria in Rwandan children.</article-title><source>Trans R Soc Trop Med Hyg</source><volume>100</volume><fpage>1105</fpage><lpage>11</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16766006</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0006358-Kamya1"><label>10</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kamya</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name><name><surname>Yeka</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Bukirwa</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Lugemwa</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Rwakimari</surname><given-names>JB</given-names></name><name><surname>Staedke</surname><given-names>SG</given-names></name><name><surname>Talisuna</surname><given-names>AO</given-names></name><name><surname>Greenhouse</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Nosten</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Rosenthal</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Wabwire-Mangen</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Dorsey</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Artemether-lumefantrine versus dihydroartemisinin-piperaquine for                        treatment of malaria: a randomized trial.</article-title><source>PLoS Clin Trials</source><volume>2(5)</volume><fpage>e20</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17525792</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0006358-Mayxay1"><label>11</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mayxay</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Thongpraseuth</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Khanthavong</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Lindegardh</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Barends</surname>